      <description>Kayode Emmanuel was parked outside the biggest hotel in Nigeria’s capital, the Transcorp Hilton Abuja, waiting for ride requests on his Uber Technologies Inc. app. When none came, he did what many Nigerians do when faced with patchy internet: he toggled his phone’s airplane mode off and back on.</description>
